difference Between IPv4 and IPv6 
let,s Talk about First IPv4 address 
                   IPv4  is a 32 bit address 
                   The 32 bits are divide in the 4 blocks of 8 bits
                    IPv4 address blocks are separated  by dot.
                    IPv4  is a numeric address . (0-255)
now let.s talk about IPv6 address 
                        IPv6 is a 128 bits
                        the 128 bits are divided into the 8 block and 16 bits
                         IPv6 address bloks are separated by the colon
                         IPv6 address is alpha-numeric address (0-9 & AF)
